description:
During May 2026, the Economic Development Department continued advancing the City of Greenacres’ vision of sustainable growth, strategic investment, business attraction, workforce development, and community engagement. Significant progress was achieved through redevelopment outreach, regional and international partnerships, business promotion initiatives, and statewide recognition of the City's innovative economic development efforts.
As Greenacres celebrates its Centennial Year, the Department remains focused on positioning the City as a destination for investment, entrepreneurship, tourism, and quality-of-life enhancements that benefit residents, businesses, and visitors alike.
1. REDEVELOPMENT AND INVESTMENT OUTREACH
Corridor Redevelopment Discussions
Throughout the month, the Department conducted targeted meetings with developers, investors, and industry stakeholders to explore redevelopment opportunities along key commercial corridors within the City. Discussions focused on mixed-use development concepts that integrate residential, retail, entertainment, hospitality, and workforce housing components. These conversations support the City’s long-term objectives of revitalizing commercial corridors, expanding economic opportunities, enhancing community amenities, and strengthening the municipal tax base. The continued interest from private-sector partners reflects growing confidence in Greenacres as an emerging destination for strategic investment and redevelopment.
Yes In God's Backyard (YIGBY) Workshop
On May 21, 2026, the Department participated in the Housing Leadership Council of Palm Beach County's YIGBY (Yes In God's Backyard) Workshop, which brought together faith-based leaders, housing developers, investors, municipal representatives, and community stakeholders to discuss innovative housing solutions and partnership opportunities. The workshop focused on YIGBY legislation, faith-based land use opportunities, affordable housing strategies, and partnership development. The Department is actively evaluating potential partnerships and development opportunities that may align with Greenacres' economic development goals while addressing housing needs within the community. These discussions provide valuable insight into emerging development models and potential investment opportunities that could support workforce housing, neighborhood revitalization, and long-term economic sustainability.
2. STRATEGIC PARTNERSHIPS AND COMMUNITY ENGAGEMENT
The Palm Beaches – Tourism and Business Networking Partnership
The City of Greenacres is proud to partner with Discover The Palm Beaches to host one of the region's premier hospitality and business networking events on June 12, 2026, at the Greenacres Community Center. This event will provide local businesses with a unique opportunity to showcase their products, services, and experiences directly to hotel concierges, front desk teams, bell staff, hospitality professionals, and tourism partners from throughout Palm Beach County. Participating businesses will have the opportunity to:
Increase visibility among tourism and hospitality professionals;
Build referral relationships that generate new customers;
Promote Greenacres as a destination for dining, shopping, and entertainment;
Share menus, samples, promotional materials, and special offers; and
Strengthen connections with regional tourism partners.
This partnership supports the City's broader efforts to elevate Greenacres' profile within Palm Beach County's visitor economy and create new opportunities for local businesses.
Mexican Consulate of Miami – Mobile Consulate Program
The Department continued coordinating with the Consulate General of Mexico in Miami to bring the Mexican Mobile Consulate Program to Greenacres on July 11, 2026. The Mobile Consulate serves as an extension of the Mexican Consulate, providing essential services directly to residents who may otherwise face barriers to accessing government resources. Services include:
Passport and Consular Identification Card issuance and renewals;
Voter registration assistance;
Civil registry services and dual-nationality documentation;
Legal and immigration information;
Health and wellness resources;
Financial literacy education; and
Community outreach services.
In addition to these services, the Department is collaborating with the Consulate to provide economic development resources related to:
Access to capital;
Business planning and entrepreneurship;
Marketing and business growth strategies;
Workforce development and employment opportunities; and
Business recruitment and investment attraction.
This partnership reflects Greenacres' commitment to supporting its diverse population while creating pathways to economic opportunity and business success.
3. BUSINESS ASSISTANCE AND BUSINESS VISIBILITY
Florida Economic Development Council Innovation in Marketing Award
On May 14, 2026, the City of Greenacres received the prestigious 2026 Innovation in Marketing Award from the Florida Economic Development Council (FEDC) during the annual IGNITE Conference in Orlando. The award recognized the City's highly successful "Dine Local. Savor Greenacres" campaign, an innovative digital marketing initiative designed to promote locally owned restaurants while highlighting the unique culinary diversity found throughout the community. The campaign combines storytelling, video marketing, and social media engagement to showcase family-owned restaurants and encourage residents and visitors to support local businesses. Since its launch, the initiative has:
Increased visibility for participating restaurants;
Expanded the City's digital reach;
Generated positive engagement across social media platforms;
Enhanced community pride; and
Strengthened Greenacres' identity as a dining destination.
Several participating businesses have reported increased customer traffic and noted that patrons specifically referenced the City's promotional videos when visiting their establishments. The success of the initiative has transformed the City's role from a traditional regulatory entity into a proactive marketing partner that helps drive economic activity and business growth. Building upon this success, the Department is expanding its business spotlight program through the launch of "Buy Local. Shop Greenacres." This new initiative will highlight locally owned retailers and unique businesses that contribute to Greenacres' economic vitality and community character. These award-winning programs exemplify the City's commitment to innovative economic development strategies that support small businesses, foster community engagement, and strengthen the local economy.
4. RECOGNITION OF PUBLIC SERVICE EXCELLENCE
Local Gov 250 – America’s Public Service Champions
The National Academy of Public Administration and LocalGov250 announced the recipients of the prestigious 250 Champions Initiative, a nationwide effort recognizing exceptional public servants whose work positively impacts communities across America. The initiative received hundreds of nominations from all 50 states, the District of Columbia, and U.S. territories. Honorees represent a diverse cross-section of government professionals who exemplify excellence, leadership, innovation, and dedication to public service. The Department is proud to share that Dr. Philip C. Harris, Director of Economic Development, was selected as one of America's 250 Public Service Champions and was among only a select group of honorees from the State of Florida recognized for outstanding contributions to local government and community development. The recognition ceremony was held in Philadelphia in conjunction with national local government leadership events celebrating public service as the United States approaches its 250th Anniversary. This honor reflects not only individual achievement but also the City of Greenacres' commitment to innovation, professional excellence, and servant leadership. The recognition brings positive national visibility to the City and highlights Greenacres as a community dedicated to advancing impactful and meaningful public service.
